Spring is a Java framework that helps you build applications by managing objects, dependencies, web requests, database access, transactions, security, and configuration for you.


What problems does Spring solve?

1. Object Management (IoC Container Inversion of Control) - Spring creates and stores objects called beans. Benefit: No manual new everywhere.

2. Dependency Injection - Spring automatically provides required dependencies. Benefit: Loose coupling and easier testing.

3. Web Framework - Spring handles HTTP requests and responses. Benefit: Easy REST API development.

4. Database Integration - Spring integrates with JDBC, Hibernate, and JPA. Benefit: Much less database boilerplate.

5. Transaction Management - Spring ensures operations succeed together or fail together. Benefit: Data consistency.

6. Security - Spring Security provides authentication and authorization. Benefit: Production-grade security.

7. Validation - Spring validates incoming data automatically. Benefit: Cleaner APIs and safer input handling.

8. Configuration Management - Different settings for development, testing, and production. Benefit: Easy deployment across environments.




The three biggest reasons companies use Spring

If you remember only three things, remember these.

1 Productivity - Build APIs in hours instead of days.

2 Maintainability - Large teams can work on cleanly separated layers.

3 Ecosystem - Security, database, messaging, cloud, testing, monitoring, batch jobs, and more work together consistently.



Spring ecosystem

Spring Core - It provides the most basic and important features of Spring. IOC, Dependency Injection, Bean Managment, configuration, ApplicationContext.

Spring MVC - used to build web applications and REST APIs. It uses Servlet technology internally but using it is easier.
Spring Data - to connect to database. Spring Data JPA - hibenate ORM
Spring Security - used for authentication and authorization
Spring AOP - Spring AOP lets you separate cross-cutting concerns (logging, transactions, security, caching, auditing, etc.) from business logic by applying code around method execution.
Spring AI - it helps java integrate AI features into spring application.



Spring Boot - Automation Layer on top of sping that configures the spring so we could start building application quickly with auto configuration, starter dependencies , embedded servers, sensible defaults, production ready features.

Maven is the build and dependency management tool for your Java/Spring Boot project.







